      "assistant_text": "According to [[write-journal]], the Guarded Write Journal page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nIn essence, it explains that before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state (its previous content if it existed, or noting that it did not exist) into an in-memory journal. If the agent run fails for any reason \u2014 whether due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or all attempted writes being denied \u2014 the journal can roll back every write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files. This provides all-or-nothing semantics for the agent\u0027s writes without requiring a database transaction, with the journal itself serving as an in-memory transaction log for the duration of one run.",
